# The PDF archive: ~141 MB, regenerable from the committed index and manifest.
# Pinned instead by data/raw/insp_sitrep_index.tsv (what exists upstream),
# data/raw/sitrep_pdfs.manifest.tsv (sha256 per file) and data/raw/PROVENANCE.tsv.
#
# THE CONTENTS ARE IGNORED, NOT THE DIRECTORY, and the difference is load-
# bearing: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so with the
# directory itself ignored the three negations below would match nothing and
# be silently inert. `data/raw/sitrep_pdfs/*` matches every entry -- regular
# file or symlink alike -- so the supported way to build without re-fetching
# 141 MB is now to link the PDFs INTO this directory one by one, which is what
# `release-check` does. (Symlinking the whole directory is no longer possible:
# it would delete three tracked files, and `make verify` would say so.)
data/raw/sitrep_pdfs/*

# EXCEPT THESE THREE, which are committed because they cannot be re-fetched
# from anywhere this project controls. INSP's media library does not list
# SitReps 001, 002 and 004 and they are not at the bare-numbered URL, so
# `make fetch` cannot bring them back; they were obtained from a secondary
# archive that has already withdrawn a different dataset without notice.
# ~7 MB of the repository, and the alternative is a working copy that loses
# the outbreak's first three observations to a `git clean`.
# registers/external_sitreps.tsv is what declares them and what the build
# checks their bytes against.
!data/raw/sitrep_pdfs/sitrep_001_2026-05-14.pdf
!data/raw/sitrep_pdfs/sitrep_002_2026-05-17.pdf
!data/raw/sitrep_pdfs/sitrep_004_2026-05-18.pdf

# Everything under build/ has a rule. Delete it and `make build` returns it.
data/build/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.snakemake/
logs/
analysis/_site/

# Trial/spike output. Regenerate with scripts/trial_geometric_table2.py.
data/trial/

# Comparison sources, cloned by `make external`; pinned by the .commit file.
# Same reason as above for the missing trailing slash.
external
analysis/data.html
analysis/*_files/
analysis/explore.html
analysis/_explore_data.json

# agent worktrees: isolated checkouts, never part of this repo
.claude/worktrees/

# Reference PDFs that are NOT ours to redistribute. This repository has a
# public remote, and the NEJM correspondence is copyright Massachusetts
# Medical Society -- not open access, unlike the two PLOS papers beside it,
# which are CC-BY and are committed. Cited in pdfs/PROVENANCE.md and in
# notes/; fetch your own copy from nejm.org.
pdfs/akilimali_et_al_2026.pdf
pdfs/akilimali_et_al_2026_supp.pdf

# The staged archives `make figures-release` builds a past release against:
# a directory of symlinks into data/raw/sitrep_pdfs plus that tag's manifest.
# (The figures themselves are under data/build/figures/<release>/, already
# ignored with the rest of data/build. They are reconstructible from the
# manifests on demand, and a set is 2.5 MB against thirty published releases.)
data/build/releases/

# Snapshots of the documents the export tables cite (`make fetch-exports`).
# Pinned by sha256 in data/raw/exports/snapshots.manifest.tsv, which is committed.
data/raw/exports/snapshots/
